# cr-rust-hello: the Rust half of milestone CR-a (docs/CR-PLAN.md, track
# CT2): a Rust program built by Chromium's pinned Rust (tools/cr/toolchain.sh
# fetches it), its standard library built from rust-src for
# x86_64-unknown-linux-musl as Chromium's GN does, and linked by the port's
# clang driver against Jam OS's musl (-C link-self-contained=no). It runs
# from /data: eight threads with thread_local destructors, channels, files,
# collections and number formatting, then (with the argument `panic`) a
# panic that aborts. Its output is the same on any Rust system:
# files/expected.txt and expected-panic.txt, which tools/cr-test.sh checks
# against the build host's own build of it and the test (`test`) against the
# Jam OS run. Jam OS's own code (`local`).
name        cr-rust-hello
version     1
revision    1
summary     a Rust test program for Jam OS's clang and Rust toolchain (CR-a)
category    tests
licence     BSD-2-Clause
licence-file LICENSE
local       files
place       package
style       custom
toolchain   clang rust
needs       llvm-runtimes
# It writes its scratch directory in /data (wants/cr-rust-hello).
program     bin/cr-rust-hello
files       share/cr-rust-hello/expected.txt share/cr-rust-hello/expected-panic.txt
